// Pins that a HYPOTHESIS-BEARING goal is refused at emission
// (2026-07-29, wave-2 release-gate audit).
//
// This row exists because the refusal is currently INCIDENTAL and is
// nonetheless relied upon. `sequentToProp` folds a sequent's
// hypotheses into a SAWCore arrow chain; the emitter does not emit
// those binders; the goal-telescope pin's ARITY half sees the
// disagreement and refuses. Nothing about that chain was designed to
// police this shape — it falls out of a dropped binder.
//
// Why it is relied upon: wave 2 argued that IF such a binder were
// emitted, its domain would be the hypothesis's `Except`-carried
// image, and an erring-but-unforced computation makes that domain
// UNINHABITED — so the implication is vacuously provable and
// `offline_lean_replay` would admit an arbitrary conclusion. That
// end-to-end claim did NOT reproduce and is logged for wave 3. Until
// it is settled, this refusal is the boundary, so it gets a row.
//
// DELIBERATELY ERROR-FREE. An earlier draft used a vector with an
// `error` in an unread slot, which would have made this row pass for
// two possible reasons at once. With no error anywhere, the ONLY
// thing that can refuse it is the shape — verified 2026-07-29 by
// running both.
//
// MUTATION: teaching the emitter to emit hypothesis binders makes the
// counts agree and this row emit cleanly. That is exactly the change
// nobody should make until the Except-carried-domain question is
// settled; this row is the tripwire.
enable_experimental;
prove_print
  (do {
     goal_cut {{ (1:[8]) == 1 }};
     goal_num_when 0 (offline_lean "hypothesis_goal");
     z3;
   })
  {{ (2:[8]) == 2 }};
